TITLE:: NdefRackUndo
summary:: cmd-z and cmd-shift-z in the rack window
categories:: Libraries>NdefRack
related:: Classes/NdefRackGUI, Classes/NdefRack

DESCRIPTION::
Every step taken in the rack window can be undone and done again. A step is one
thing done there: a mouse press to its release (a drag, a cable, a bar, a
click), a key, a menu item, a value typed, a module made from the library.

Nothing has to say what a step does. The rack as it was before is compared with
the rack as it is after, and whatever differs is the step:

table::
## strong::what:: || strong::set back with::
## modules deleted || made again from what link::Classes/NdefRack#*removeAll:: wrote down: names, sources, values, places, cables, playing
## modules made || taken out, written down first so that redo makes them again
## cables and values || control by control, as the node map held them: a cable is plugged in again, unplugging is unplugging (unmap, then set)
## voices, a bus, speakers || the source slot 0 had, put the way the rack changes it, so what the module feeds stays patched
## playing || played or stopped
## the window's marks || places, bends, network boxes, comments, colours, compact, pages, hidden modules
::

Only what the step changed goes back. A control that a controller or your code
moved since the step is left where it is, unless the step moved it too. Changes
made in code or by a controller are never steps of their own: the rack stores no
patch, and undo keeps only what the window did to it. Triggers are never set
back, since setting one fires it.

The window calls link::#*undo:: on cmd-z and link::#*redo:: on cmd-shift-z; its
canvas menu offers both by name. At most link::#*maxSteps:: steps are kept.

code::
// a step of your own, undone by the window's cmd-z like any other
NdefRackUndo.step { NdefRack.moveTo(\osc, Point(300, 40)); NdefRack.setColor(\osc, \teal) };
NdefRackUndo.undoName;   // what cmd-z would undo, in words
NdefRackUndo.undo;
NdefRackUndo.redo;
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: step
Run a function as one step. Inside another step, it is part of that one.
ARGUMENT:: func
what to do
RETURNS:: what the function returns

METHOD:: begin
Start a step by hand; link::#*end:: closes it. Calls nest: only the outermost
pair makes a step.

METHOD:: end
Close a step begun with link::#*begin::.

METHOD:: gestureBegin
A mouse press in the window: a step until link::#*gestureEnd::, closing first
whatever an earlier press left open (a release that a menu took).

METHOD:: gestureEnd
The release: the step closed.

METHOD:: flush
Close whatever step is open now.

METHOD:: noteRemoved
Called by link::Classes/NdefRack#*removeAll:: with what it wrote down, so that
undo can make the modules again.
ARGUMENT:: snap
the removal's snapshot

METHOD:: undo
Take the last step back.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Event:: - code::name:: what it was, code::keys:: the
modules it made again - or nil when there is nothing to undo

METHOD:: redo
Do the last step undone again.
RETURNS:: the same as link::#*undo::

METHOD:: canUndo
METHOD:: canRedo
Whether there is a step to undo, to redo.

METHOD:: undoName
METHOD:: redoName
What undo or redo would take back or do again, in a few words; nil for nothing.

METHOD:: undoList
METHOD:: redoList
The steps, the last one last.

METHOD:: maxSteps
How many steps are kept: 100.

METHOD:: clear
Forget every step.
